requirements.requirement:
Every external model artefact must support provenance such as:

{
  "source": {
    "system": "Archetype Designer",
    "artifactType": "DESIGNER_AUTHORING_JSON",
    "sourceRevision": "...",
    "exportedAt": "...",
    "importedAt": "..."
  },
  "content": {
    "hash": "...",
    "mediaType": "...",
    "filename": "..."
  },
  "repository": {
    "project": "...",
    "revision": "..."
  }
}

Preserve source-specific metadata without contaminating the generic openEHR domain model.

Return explicit validation evidence.

Example:

{
  "artifact": "...",
  "validation": {
    "syntax": "PASS",
    "structure": "PASS",
    "openehrSemantics": "PASS",
    "terminology": "PASS"
  }
}

Only report checks that were actually executed.

Represent external tool capabilities.

Example:

{
  "provider": "archetype-designer",
  "capabilities": {
    "import": true,
    "exportOet": true,
    "exportOpt": false,
    "apiAccess": false,
    "automatedRelease": false
  }
}

Actual values must come from verified capability detection/configuration.

Migrated artefacts should record that provenance metadata was created retrospectively.

Example:

{
  "provenance": {
    "origin": "UNKNOWN",
    "migration": {
      "migrated": true,
      "migrationVersion": "...",
      "migratedAt": "...",
      "originalRepositoryRevision": "..."
    }
  }
}

Do not make retrospectively generated provenance appear contemporaneous with the original model creation.
